{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And they shall not come to look as the holy is swallowed down.</b> The expression כבלע means the removal and nullification of a thing; and likewise (Habakkuk 3:3) ״ודרך אורחותיך בלעו״." "<b>And by way of</b> the plain sense (peshat): it says, 'and they shall not come to look when its structure is dismantled and the curtain-screen is removed, and then the ark, which is holy, is revealed' — as if it said, 'and they shall not come to look at the holy as it is swallowed down.'" "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'and they shall not come to look כבלע' — when the Glory is swallowed and returns to its first place, to the holy above.'" "<b>And you should know</b> that all through the year the Glory would slip from the cloud into the innermost sanctuary completely and be revealed upon the kapporet. This is what is written (Leviticus 16:2): ״כי בענן אראה על הכפרת״ — it did not say 'כי אראה בענן' but said 'כי בענן אראה', meaning: I come in a pillar of cloud and afterward I am heard from the cloud and appear upon the kapporet. I have already alluded to this in its place. Therefore the High Priest had no permission to enter there except once a year, on Yom HaKippurim, and even on Yom HaKippurim he is not permitted to enter there except with the incense — not that he brings the incense already made, but that he prepares it there and its smoke rises there and the Glory is concealed from his eyes, as it is written (ibid.): ״וכסה ענן הקטורת את הכפרת״. And this is why he warned the Levites: 'and they shall not come to look' when the Glory is swallowed into the holy, which is 'the hiding of His might' (חביון עזו); as it is written (Habakkuk 3:4): ״ונוגה כאור תהיה קרנים מידו לו ושם חביון עזו״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {3 "Comment [0] cites Habakkuk 3:3, but the verse referenced ('ודרך אורחותיך בלעו') is Deuteronomy 33:3 in many editions (cf. Rashi ad loc., who cites it as דברי הימים); however the phrase appears in Habakkuk 3:3 in some manuscripts. The printed citation reads 'שם ג' which could point to either book chapter 3; left ambiguous as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:33.698552799Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}